# Responsive Design

Whenever you implement or change any UI/design, you MUST verify responsiveness
BEFORE reporting the task as done. Do not finish a UI change without this check,
so we avoid back-and-forth fixes.

## Rules
- Mobile-first: write base styles for small screens, then layer `sm:` `md:` `lg:` `xl:`.
- Grids/flex must reflow, never overflow. Prefer `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`.
- Avoid fixed pixel widths that break mobile. Use `w-full`, `max-w-*`, and `min-w-0`.
- Long text must wrap or truncate (`truncate`, `break-words`).
- Touch targets ≥ 40px on mobile.

## Example
```tsx
// ❌ BAD: fixed grid, breaks on phones
<div className="grid grid-cols-5 gap-4">

// ✅ GOOD: reflows across breakpoints
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-5 gap-4">
```

When reporting the change, state which breakpoints you accounted for
(e.g. ~375px phone, ~768px tablet, ≥1280px desktop).
